# M-package-manager step 3b (lane pm-fetch's finding, 2026-11-08): the
# catalogue's `git = "file://packages/yaml"` writes a path where `file://`
# reads a host, and `heroes fetch` refuses it, `source_refused`; the build read
# the line and said the package was not placed, *`heroes fetch` places it*,
# sending the author to the verb that refuses it. The reader asks the address
# the rule the verb asks, `fetch/address.hero`'s `shaped`, and the build
# refuses the line with that rule's code and words, as the verb does.
use <yaml>/load  #~ source_refused

function main()
    print(load.size())
